---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { posts, dateLabel } from '../lib/writing';
---
<Base>
<div class="reading">
<p class="eyebrow">Education · Community · Chicago</p>
<h1>Hi, I’m Jake.</h1>
<p class="lead">I work to make sure every computer science teacher has a community they can rely on.</p>
<p>I’m the Executive Director of the <a href="https://csteachers.org/">Computer Science Teachers Association</a>. Before that, I taught high school computer science in Chicago and worked at Code.org.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/about/">A little more about me <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</div>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
<div class="section-top"><h2 id="writing-title" class="section-label">Writing</h2><a class="small-link" href="/writing/">All writing <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
{posts.length ? posts.slice(0,3).map(post => <article class="post-row"><time datetime={new Date(post.frontmatter.date).toISOString()}>{dateLabel(post.frontmatter.date)}</time><h2><a href={`/writing/${post.slug}/`}>{post.frontmatter.title}</a></h2><p>{post.frontmatter.description}</p></article>) : <div class="reading"><h2>A place for longer thoughts.<br />And shorter ones, too.</h2><p class="muted">I’m making room here for essays and notes. There’s nothing published yet. When there is, you’ll find it here.</p><a class="text-link" href="/feed.xml">Follow along via RSS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>}
</section>
</Base>
